WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.787
Let’s begin with intentionally messy data.

00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:06.017
Order ID two appears twice.

00:00:06.017 --> 00:00:12.452
Channel labels use different capitalization and spacing, and one channel is missing.

00:00:12.452 --> 00:00:20.602
Amount contains numeric-looking text, a missing value, and an unusually large value of nine hundred ninety-nine.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.852
The dtypes output is also important.

00:00:23.852 --> 00:00:31.017
Because amount contains strings and missing data, Pandas may not treat the column as a clean numeric type.

00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:35.852
This is what real data often looks like before preparation begins.
